## ❌ ANTI-PATTERNS (FORBIDDEN)

| Anti-Pattern | Why Wrong | Correct Approach |
|--------------|-----------|------------------|
| Using Python/Bash for artifact extraction | Misses nested details, inconsistent | Use Read tool directly |
| Generating without INVENTORY step | No baseline count to verify against | Count elements first, COMMIT to N (RGV §1) |
| Proceeding without VERIFY step | Missed elements go undetected | Count generated items, compare to N (RGV §1) |
| Summarized/abbreviated mapping tables | Data loss — mappings used for migration | Document ALL mappings, every row |
| Assuming NDF subtype from file path | Path does not determine content type | Read NDF content, classify from attributes |
| Skipping extensionless files | Misses WSDL and policy artifacts | Read content to determine type |
| Generic flow step descriptions | Loses implementation detail | Full properties, connectivity, pipeline effects per step |
| Separate "connections" section in flow docs | Disconnects steps from their connectivity | Embed connectivity per component |
| Verification counts in main document | Clutters specification output | Counts go ONLY in verification-checklist.md |
| Generating from stale Phase 0 context | Phase 0 reads are for classification only | RE-READ fresh before every section |
| Inferring behavior not in artifacts | Zero-assumption violation | Document only what EXISTS in the files |
| Skipping "obvious" NDF properties | Data loss for migration use case | Extract ALL properties and fields |
| Mixing governance metadata with runtime facts | Noise in specification | Separate; only include runtime-impacting facts |
| Asking "Should I continue?" between phases | Disrupts continuous workflow | Auto-proceed with micro-checkpoints |

### Phase Boundary Anti-Patterns
```
❌ Generating cross-artifact synthesis before completing Phases 1-4
❌ Generating verification before completing Phase 5
❌ "Should I continue with Phase 2?"
❌ "Ready to proceed to Phase 3?"
❌ "Would you like me to continue?"
❌ "I'll proceed while waiting..."
❌ "Assuming you agree..."
❌ Making assumptions about missing artifact data
❌ Inferring behavior not explicit in artifact files
```

